# Application configuration. Copy to iobio.env on the server.
#
# The backend reads config.json and overrides it from IOBIO_GENE_*,
# IOBIO_BAM_* and IOBIO_BACKEND_* variables, then serves the result at
# /config.json. Exact values true and false become JSON booleans; everything
# else stays a string.
#
# Docker passes these through verbatim: do NOT quote values, or the quotes
# become part of the value. Each value runs to the end of the line.
#
# IOBIO_BACKEND_ORIGIN is set by docker-stack.yml from DOMAIN. Don't set it here.

# Route layout. The gene app is served at the domain root; the backend API is
# mounted under /api. Anything left at "/" satisfies the container healthcheck.
IOBIO_GENE_PATH_PREFIX=/
IOBIO_BACKEND_PATH_PREFIX=/api

IOBIO_GENE_SITE_NAME=Example Genomics
IOBIO_GENE_DEFAULT_MODE=advanced
IOBIO_GENE_SHOW_INTRO=false
IOBIO_GENE_SHOW_FILES_BUTTON=false
IOBIO_GENE_SHOW_BLOGS_AND_TUTORIALS=false
IOBIO_GENE_PHENOLYZER_PERMITTED=true

# Leave empty to disable OMIM lookups.
IOBIO_GENE_OMIM_API_KEY=

IOBIO_GENE_INTRO_PARAGRAPH_1=This gene analysis tool enables you to examine any gene in your genome and identify variants that may have clinical significance.
IOBIO_GENE_INTRO_PARAGRAPH_2=To get started, enter a gene name (e.g. BRCA2) into the search field in the navigation bar. You can also click on the 'Gene panel' button to the right to examine multiple genes at once. In the panel on the left, you will then see a list of all genes that you searched for. Click on a gene to examine it.
IOBIO_GENE_INTRO_PARAGRAPH_3=This will bring up a 'Variants' panel. It shows the genetic variants that you have in the selected gene. Different types of variants are represented using icons of different shapes and colors. A legend with explanations is located in the left bottom corner. Click on a variant icon to open the 'Variant' panel with more information on the variant. When the gene analysis tool detects important variants, they are shown in a list of variants on the left.
IOBIO_GENE_INTRO_PARAGRAPH_4=
